10 REM KALEIDOSCOPE - MACHINE CODE DRAWS, BASIC ASKS
20 REM BLOCK AT 768, PARAMETERS IN ITS FIRST THREE BYTES, ENTRY CALL 771
30 TEXT
40 HOME
50 INPUT "SEED (0-255)";S
60 INPUT "TWIST (0-255)";T
70 INPUT "PASSES (1-9)";N
80 IF N < 1 THEN N = 1
90 IF N > 9 THEN N = 9
100 REM APPLESOFT HAS NO MOD, SO THE BYTES ARE WRAPPED THE LONG WAY ROUND
110 POKE 768,ABS (S) - 256 * INT ( ABS (S) / 256)
120 POKE 769,ABS (T) - 256 * INT ( ABS (T) / 256)
130 POKE 770,N
140 REM HGR CLEARS HI-RES PAGE 1, WHICH IS WHERE THE ROUTINE DRAWS
150 HGR
160 CALL 771
170 REM PEEK ( - 16384) IS THE WAIT: GET WOULD DO, BUT IT ECHOES INTO THE FOUR
180 REM TEXT LINES UNDER THE PICTURE
190 K = PEEK ( - 16384)
200 IF K < 128 THEN 190
210 POKE - 16368,0
220 GOTO 30
